The '''1998 Idaho gubernatorial election''' was held on November 3, 1998, to elect the [[Governor of Idaho]]. [[Phil Batt]], the [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] incumbent, chose not to run for a second term. The Republican nominee, United States Senator [[Dirk Kempthorne]], handily defeated the [[Republican Party (United States)|Democratic]] nominee, former Idaho Supreme Court justice [[Robert C. Huntley]], to keep the seat in GOP hands.

